Solution: The static power is P static (0.040 A)(1.2 V) 48mW. If the phone is not being used, this is the only power consumption, so the battery life is (6Whr)/(0.048 W) 125 hours (about 5 days). If the phone is being used, the dynamic power is P dynamic (0.5)(10 8 F)(1.2 V) 2 (3 10 8 Hz) 2.16 W. Together with the static and broadcast power, the total active power is 2.16W 0.048 W 3W 5.2W, so the battery life is 6W-hr/5.2W 1.15 hours. This example somewhat oversimplifies the actual operation of a cell phone, but it illustrates the key ideas of power consumption.



